{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963584,"nonce":"NoDssgsYgtEglJhBTBRkYpN+v/8=","title":"Generic call inference drops every type argument on Null\u003cInt\u003e/Null\u003cFloat\u003e and UInt/Int pairs","message":"Rows: Issue2663, Issue2736.\n\n`infer_call_type_arguments` (tast/ast_lowering/expr/calls.rs) merges only a bare Int/Float pair\ninto Float. `show\u003cT\u003e(b, a)` with `b:Null\u003cFloat\u003e`, `a:Null\u003cInt\u003e` (or UInt vs Int) returns no type\narguments, `widen_int_literals_for_type_args` never runs, the monomorphizer logs \"cannot infer\ntype_param 'T'\", and the erased body reads the Int argument's bits as a Float (prints 4.9e-324).\n\nIssue2736 reaches the same place because ast_lowering/infer.rs types an abstract binary op as its\nLHS type: `UInt / UInt` is typed UInt although `@:op(A/B)` returns Float. Further UInt gaps in\nthat row:\n- tast_to_hir.rs `seed_class_operator_methods` keeps the first overload per (abstract, operator);\n  `b == 50000.0` calls `equalsInt`;\n- `a \u003e 1.0` converts with a signed `i32-\u003ef64`; UInt prints signed.","files":null}]}